NAME
    vcc - the VNU C compiler

SYNOPSIS
    vcc [-c] [-o out] [-I dir] file.c [file.o] [file.a]

DESCRIPTION
    Compiles and links C programs for VNU: a preprocessor, a compiler
    for a strict i386 C subset into ELF relocatable objects, and a
    linker that links against the standard library (crt0.o plus
    libvlibc.a, read from /lib). The whole compiler runs inside the OS
    and writes its output to the VFS, so a simple
        vcc hello.c -o a.out
    produces a VNU executable.

    Flags are appended in any order. With -c only the relocatable
    object is written (default file a.o); without it vcc compiles the
    single .c file and links it with crt0.o and the whole libvlibc.a
    into a full VNU ELF (default a.out). Object files may be linked
    individually through a lib.a archive.

    Input sources are read from the VFS; no files larger than memory
    are expected. vcc is itself compiled with vcc (it is self-hosting).

OPTIONS
    -c            compile only, write the object file
    -o out        output file (default a.o with -c, else a.out)
    -I dir        add dir to the include search path
        --help    display this help and exit
        --version output version information and exit

EXAMPLES
    vcc -c hello.c -o hello.o
    vcc main.c libfoo.a -o app          link app from main.c and the
                                        archive

FILES
    /lib/crt0.o     startup object
    /lib/libvlibc.a standard C library archive

EXIT STATUS
    0 on success, 1 on any compile, link or I/O error.
